cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AncestryAudit, please cite it as below."
title: "AncestryAudit: Auditing and improving cancer genomic models for Asian patients"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yergaliyeva
    given-names: Dana
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanYerga/ancestryaudit"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/ancestryaudit/"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python library that tests whether an accuracy gap between
  patient populations is statistically significant, estimates the smallest gap
  the data can detect, and checks whether cancer-type or subtype composition
  explains the gap before any correction is applied.
keywords:
  - cancer genomics
  - fairness
  - machine learning
  - copy-number variation
  - TCGA
